# Wave 14: fix ttm/grid (same arguments; serial run must reproduce fix ttm), heat diffusion with sub-stepping (docs.lammps.org/fix_ttm.html: the electron equation
# is "C_e rho_e dT_e/dt = div(kappa_e grad T_e) - g_p (T_e - T_a) + g_s T_a'"). Small C_e (0.001) so that
# the atom coupling is visible in the electron energy; kappa_e 0.01 on a 2x2x2 grid with timestep 0.2 gives
# a diffusion number above 1/2, so each step is split into sub-steps. Two runs, infile start.
# oracle-inputs: w14ttm_grid.init
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         sc 3.0
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 10.0
displace_atoms  all move 0.5 0.5 0.5 units box
variable        vx atom 3.0*sin(0.9*x+0.4*y)
variable        vy atom 2.5*cos(0.7*y-0.5*z)
variable        vz atom 2.0*sin(1.1*z+0.3*x)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
velocity        all zero linear
pair_style      lj/cut 3.0
pair_coeff      1 1 0.0 2.0
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all ttm/grid 777 0.001 1.0 0.01 20.0 0.0 2.0 2 2 2 infile w14ttm_grid.init
timestep        0.2
thermo_style    custom step temp pe f_2[1] f_2[2]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          1
run             3
run             2
